cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the scientific sources of each record and upstream software implementations as appropriate; this citation describes the catalog software."
title: "Electrochemical Battery Parameters"
type: software
abstract: >-
  E-BatP is a traceable reference catalog of lithium-ion battery parameters and
  experimental records for DFN/P2D, SPM and SPMe modeling. It includes electrode
  open-circuit potential curves, diffusion, reaction kinetics, geometry, transport
  and thermal parameters, with full-cell test links where supported by evidence.
  Records preserve source definitions, reuse licenses, cell and study matching
  levels, and missing data. Entries can be partial references. The project curates
  and exports data; it does not run model simulations or report predictive
  performance. Individual data sources retain their own licenses and citation
  requirements.
keywords:
  - electrochemistry
  - lithium-ion batteries
  - battery modeling
  - electrochemical parameters
  - battery datasets
  - PyBaMM
  - DFN
  - P2D
  - SPM
  - SPMe
  - open-circuit potential
  - OCP
  - GITT
  - solid-state diffusion
  - reaction kinetics
  - exchange current density
  - LFP
  - NMC
  - full-cell testing
  - data provenance
  - NCA
  - electrochemical impedance spectroscopy
  - EIS
  - US06
  - UDDS
  - WLTP
  - multi-rate charge/discharge
